---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Base
  title="Title IX and civil rights"
  description="How to reach the University of Mars Title IX coordinator and what happens after a report."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Office for Civil Rights"
    title="Title IX &amp; civil rights"
    lede="The university prohibits sexual harassment, sexual violence, and discrimination in its programs. You can report without deciding what should happen next."
    crumbs={[{ href: '/title-ix/', label: 'Title IX' }]}
  >
    <p class="page-actions">
      <a class="btn" href={`mailto:${site.titleEmail}`}>Contact the Title IX coordinator</a>
    </p>
  </PageHero>
  <article class="prose wrap narrow">
    <h2>How to report</h2>
    <p>
      Write or call the Title IX coordinator. If you are in immediate danger, call campus safety at
      <a href={site.safetyHref}>{site.safetyPhone}</a> or local emergency services first.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.titleEmail}`}>{site.titleEmail}</a></li>
      <li>Phone: <a href={site.titleHref}>{site.titlePhone}</a>, weekdays 9 a.m. to 5 p.m.</li>
      <li>Office: Enrollment Services, Room 210, {site.street}</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>What happens next</h2>
    <p>
      A coordinator will respond within one business day. They will explain confidential resources, supportive measures
      such as a housing or class change, and the choice to request an investigation. You may bring a support person to
      any meeting. Retaliation for reporting is prohibited.
    </p>
    <h2>Confidential help</h2>
    <p>
      Counseling at University Health Services and the campus advocacy office can talk with you without filing a Title IX
      report. They will explain the limits of that confidentiality, including a duty to act if a minor is at risk.
    </p>
    <p>
      The university does not discriminate in education or employment. A longer statement is in the footer of every page.
      Employment complaints may also go to human resources.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
